---
description: Repository-wide operating standard for all Cursor-driven work.
alwaysApply: true
---

Use `docs/agents/agent-operating-standard.md` as the source of truth for how to work in this repository.

- Map each request to exactly one `scenario_id`.
- Read `docs/agents/context-loading-policy.md` and keep the root context minimal.
- Read the matching `docs/harness/scenarios/*.md` file before changing LLM behavior.
- Treat `docs/harness/*` as the canonical harness standard.
- Treat `docs/ops/sprint-workflow.md` and `docs/ops/learnings-and-checkpoints.md` as the canonical workflow and reflection standard.
- Do not preload unrelated scenario docs or domain descriptions.
- If prompt/workflow/retrieval/guardrail/trace/export behavior changes, update eval and release-gate surfaces too.
- Do not modify `legacy_ai_portal_prototype/` unless explicitly asked.
- Do not run `git commit` or `git push` unless explicitly asked.
- Keep responses and summaries explicit about `scenario_id`, changed surfaces, required regressions, and open risks.
- Search existing official docs or known patterns before inventing unfamiliar runtime or infrastructure designs.
